{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "id": "typicality-by-counting",
  "title": {
    "zh": "计数中的典型",
    "en": "Typicality by counting"
  },
  "kind": "theorem",
  "status": "recorded-checked",
  "family": "F01",
  "reviewed_at_utc": "2026-10-16T00:00:00+00:00",
  "statement": {
    "zh": "计数给出多数历程显示权重：两个值以自然数权重 p、q 计数，n 步历程加权的平方偏差恰好加起来是 n·p·q·(p + q)ⁿ，偏差大的历程所占之重随 n 下降。发生的是哪一个历程，在计数所定之外。",
    "en": "Counting shows that most courses show the weights: with natural weights p and q on two values, the weighted squared deviations of the courses of n steps add up exactly to n·p·q·(p + q)ⁿ, so the courses far off weigh a share that falls with n. Which course happens lies outside what counting decides."
  },
  "laws": [
    {
      "zh": "n 步的历程恰是 n 个值的列表，共 2ⁿ 个；每个一计 p、每个零计 q，合起来重 (p + q)ⁿ。",
      "en": "The courses of n steps are exactly the lists of n values, 2ⁿ of them; weighing p for each one and q for each zero, they weigh (p + q)ⁿ together.",
      "declarations": [
        "Becoming.Typicality.ones",
        "Becoming.Typicality.zeros",
        "Becoming.Typicality.weight",
        "Becoming.Typicality.courses",
        "Becoming.Typicality.total",
        "Becoming.Typicality.mem_courses_iff",
        "Becoming.Typicality.courses_length",
        "Becoming.Typicality.total_weight"
      ]
    },
    {
      "zh": "平方偏差之和恰好：a 个一、b 个零的历程以 x = q·a、y = p·b 读，n 步历程加权的 x·x + y·y 之和，是加权的 2·x·y 之和加 n·p·q·(p + q)ⁿ；每一步加 p·q·(p + q) 乘其权重，无论之前如何。",
      "en": "The spread is exact: reading a course with a ones and b zeros by x = q·a and y = p·b, the weighted x·x + y·y summed over the courses of n steps is the weighted 2·x·y summed plus n·p·q·(p + q)ⁿ; each step adds p·q·(p + q) times the weight, whatever came before.",
      "declarations": [
        "Becoming.Typicality.ahead",
        "Becoming.Typicality.behind",
        "Becoming.Typicality.square",
        "Becoming.Typicality.cross",
        "Becoming.Typicality.steps_leave",
        "Becoming.Typicality.spread"
      ]
    },
    {
      "zh": "多数历程显示权重：x·x + y·y ≥ 2·x·y + d 的历程之重乘 d 至多 n·p·q·(p + q)ⁿ；所以一的频率与 p / (p + q) 相差 ε 以上者，所占之重至多 p·q / ((p + q)²·ε²·n)。",
      "en": "Most courses show the weights: those with x·x + y·y ≥ 2·x·y + d weigh, times d, at most n·p·q·(p + q)ⁿ; so those whose frequency of ones is off p / (p + q) by ε or more weigh a share of at most p·q / ((p + q)²·ε²·n).",
      "declarations": [
        "Becoming.Typicality.two_mul_le",
        "Becoming.Typicality.offBy",
        "Becoming.Typicality.offBy_le",
        "Becoming.Typicality.typical"
      ]
    },
    {
      "zh": "权重就是历史之和的权重：以计数加权的自由分支沿每个历史复合的就是这里的权重，n 步历史之和就是这里的总重。",
      "en": "The weights are those of the sum over histories: free branching weighted by counting composes along each history the weight here, and its sum over the histories of n steps is the total weight here.",
      "declarations": [
        "Becoming.Typicality.stepWeight",
        "Becoming.Typicality.along_weight",
        "Becoming.Typicality.transfer_weight",
        "Becoming.Typicality.sum_courses_weight"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "zh": "不加公理，不加前提：两个值与自然数权重 p、q 写在每条定理中；实数权重属于外围。",
      "en": "No axiom and no premise: two values and natural weights p and q, written into each theorem; real weights belong to the periphery."
    }
  ],
  "does_not_show": [
    {
      "zh": "发生的历程是典型的：每个历程都是自由分支的一个运行，全是一的历程亦然；把权重读作机会者加上这一前提。",
      "en": "That the course which happens is typical: every course is a run of free branching, the all-ones course among them; reading weights as chances adds this premise.",
      "kind": "correspondence"
    },
    {
      "zh": "指数的集中（Chernoff）、多于两个值与非自然数的权重。",
      "en": "Exponential concentration (Chernoff), more than two values, and weights that are not natural numbers.",
      "kind": "scope"
    }
  ],
  "counterexamples": [],
