  "next_delta": {
    "zh": "指数之界的集中与多于两个值；外围中实数权重作为实例；Ren 对读法的判断（概率是计数加上“发生的历程是典型的”这一前提）。",
    "en": "Concentration with exponential bounds, and more than two values; real weights in the periphery as an instance; Ren's judgment on the reading (probability as counting plus the premise that the course which happens is typical)."
  },
  "correspondence": {
    "zh": "Ren 2026-10-15：“\"What this line doesn’t reach\" is also worth doing”，其中之一是有概率的世界。已知的结果：二项分布的切比雪夫不等式（伯努利的弱大数定律）。这里在核心中不用公理地给出，接到 Becoming.Weighted 的计数权重，并标出不被推出的前提。读法（AI 的，待 Ren）：权重是在历程之间计数的，不是一个历程所识的；记录显示权重，恰在发生的历程典型之处，而计数只说多数典型；概率的读法正在于加上这一前提。",
    "en": "Ren, 15 October 2026: “\"What this line doesn’t reach\" is also worth doing”, worlds with probability among it. Known result: Chebyshev's inequality for the binomial (Bernoulli's weak law of large numbers). Here it is given in the core with no axiom, joined to the counting weights of Becoming.Weighted, and the premise not derived is marked. Readings (the AI's, pending Ren): weights are counted across courses, not registered in one; a record shows the weights exactly where the course that happens is typical, and counting says only that most are; the reading of probability lies in adding that premise."
  },
